# NOTE: models/*.pt and models/*.sha256 are intentionally tracked, not
# ignored -- a previous pass here ignored them as "repo bloat," but
# they're tiny (the two current models are ~7KB/~99KB combined) and the
# whole pipeline requires them to exist on a fresh checkout: tests load
# them, the Dockerfile bakes them into the image, and CI's
# integrity-verification step needs their .sha256 alongside them.
# Untracking them broke exactly that on the next clean CI run.
#
# models/*.sig was a stale fake artifact (a hex digest, not a real
# signature) from before real signing existed and has been removed. Real
# model provenance is now a cosign KEYLESS signature bundle, generated
# fresh and verified in every CI run (see .github/workflows/ci.yml) --
# not a static file meant to be committed.
models/*.cosign.bundle
